{
  "id": "ep240",
  "duration": 48.764,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.672,
      "text": "Inside a normal red giant star, a dead neutron star is buried.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Betelgeuse and Siwarha.png",
        "credit": "WhirligigGirl",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betelgeuse_and_Siwarha.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.733,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.733,
          "end": 4.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.672,
      "end": 9.342,
      "text": "Most astronomers once assumed such hybrid stars were impossible.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ESO - Milky Way.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/S. Brunier",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ESO_-_Milky_Way.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.667,
          "end": 7.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.133,
          "end": 9.333,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.342,
      "end": 15.837,
      "text": "In nineteen seventy-seven, Kip Thorne and Anna \u017bytkow first hypothesized these bizarre objects.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Neutron star cross section.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neutron_star_cross_section.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.333,
          "end": 15.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.837,
      "end": 23.157,
      "text": "Theoretical models show the embedded core reaches extreme temperatures exceeding ten to the nine Kelvin.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustrations of Disks around Black Holes (2005-bhlock-more-2 - bhdisk ill).tiff",
        "credit": "(Credit: NASA/CXC/M.Weiss)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustrations_of_Disks_around_Black_Holes_(2005-bhlock-more-2_-_bhdisk_ill).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.833,
          "end": 23.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.157,
      "end": 29.002,
      "text": "Between twenty and two hundred of these strange hybrids may exist across the Milky Way.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.167,
          "end": 29.0,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.002,
      "end": 37.702,
      "text": "In twenty fourteen, astronomers identified the star HV twenty eleven two in the Small Magellanic Cloud as a candidate.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Small Magellanic Cloud (ground-based image) (heic0603d).jpg",
        "credit": "ESA/Hubble and Digitized Sky Survey 2. Acknowledgements: Davide De Martin",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Small_Magellanic_Cloud_(ground-based_image)_(heic0603d).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.0,
          "end": 32.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.467,
          "end": 37.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.702,
      "end": 45.497,
      "text": "Yet confirming this hidden core is buried inside requires detecting both unique light and gravitational waves.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "MergingBlackHoles V2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Ames Research Center/C. Henze",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MergingBlackHoles_V2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.7,
          "end": 45.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 45.497,
      "end": 48.414,
      "text": "Proving that a dead neutron star is buried.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Betelgeuse and Siwarha.png",
        "credit": "WhirligigGirl",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betelgeuse_and_Siwarha.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 45.5,
          "end": 48.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
